{"name":"Plus Ultra","hex":"#78ac01","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["And; sum of the previous one and the following one.","With; having in addition."]},{"part":"Conjunction","definitions":["And also; in addition; besides (which)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plus"},{"term":"ultra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extreme; far beyond the norm; fanatical; uncompromising."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A political extremist, in particular:\n\nAn ultraleftist.\nAn ultranationalist.\n An ultraroyalist.","An ultraleftist."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plus ultra","blocks":[{"text":"Plus ultra is a Latin phrase and the national motto of Spain. A reversal of the original phrase non plus ultra, said to have been inscribed as a warning on the Pillars of Hercules at the Strait of Gibraltar, it has metaphorical suggestions of taking risks and striving for excellence. Its original version, the personal motto of the Holy Roman Emperor Charles V, also Duke of Burgundy and King of Spain, was Plus oultre in French. It appears on the columns of the Spanish coat of arms, in reference to the discovery of the New World."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Escudo_de_Espa%C3%B1a_%28variant%29.svg/330px-Escudo_de_Espa%C3%B1a_%28variant%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plus_ultra","wikidata":"Q1045726"},{"title":"Plus Ultra (aircraft)","blocks":[{"text":"Plus Ultra is a Dornier Do J flying boat which completed the first transatlantic flight between Spain and South America in January 1926 with a crew of Spanish aviators which included Major Ramón Franco, Captain Julio Ruiz de Alda Miqueleiz, Sub-Lieutenant Juan Manuel Durán, and the mechanic Pablo Rada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/PlusUtraPalos.jpg/330px-PlusUtraPalos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plus_Ultra_(aircraft)","wikidata":"Q1195128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Plusoultre.jpg/500px-Plusoultre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Plusoultre.jpg/500px-Plusoultre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wooden panelling in Charles V's palace in the Alhambra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlusoultre.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/PlusOultreBinche.jpg/500px-PlusOultreBinche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/PlusOultreBinche.jpg/1280px-PlusOultreBinche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/PlusOultreBinche.jpg/500px-PlusOultreBinche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Motto of the city of Binche, Belgium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlusOultreBinche.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG/500px-Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG/1280px-Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG/500px-Tripul_Plus_Ultra.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crew of the Plus Ultra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A